In `_faceIjkPentToCellBoundary`:
```c
g->numVerts = 0;
FaceIJK lastFijk;  // uninitialized
for (int vert = start; vert < start + length + additionalIteration; vert++) {
    int v = vert % NUM_PENT_VERTS;
    FaceIJK fijk = fijkVerts[v];
    _adjustPentVertOverage(&fijk, adjRes);
    if (isResolutionClassIII(res) && vert > start) {
        // Uses lastFijk here
        ...
    }
    ...
    lastFijk = fijk;
}
```

When `start > 0` and `vert == start`, the condition `vert > start` is false, so `lastFijk` is not read on the first iteration. But on the second iteration (`vert == start + 1`), `lastFijk` was set to `fijk` from the first iteration. So `lastFijk` is always initialized before use in this loop.

